Author: opencode-coder <opencode-coder@localhost>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 23:49:55 2026 +0000

    feat: allow a public-DID override for proxy-signed identities
    
    Add GITLAWB_PROXY_DID: when set, a Keypair presents that DID instead of
    the one derived from its local PEM, while signatures stay made by the
    local key. Deployments with a trusted signing proxy use this so a coding
    box holds a disposable key and the proxy re-signs each request with the
    real private key, which never leaves the proxy.
    
    - gitlawb-core: Keypair.public_did override + apply_proxy_did_from_env
    - gl: override applied in load_keypair_from_dir; identity sign/export
      warn (local PEM is not the real key); issue create omits the optional
      signed_payload in proxy mode
    - git-remote-gitlawb: same override for clone/fetch/push; env documented
      in --help
    
    Behavior is unchanged when GITLAWB_PROXY_DID is not set.

